WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.500
[gentle music]

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.440
Welcome to the world of chiplets,

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.960
a breakthrough in semiconductor
design that enhances scalability,

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.580
performance, and cost efficiency.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.900
For decades, Moore's Law has
driven chip advancements,

6
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.940
doubling transistor
counts every two years.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.980
However, as chips become
larger and more complex,

8
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.120
they face manufacturing limits,
lower yields, and increased costs.

9
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.230
Expanding chip size or increasing

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.760
transistor density has become
increasingly difficult.

11
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.880
A new approach is needed,
one that enables scalability,

12
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.880
flexibility, and cost savings.

13
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.640
Instead of a single massive chip,

14
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.920
chiplets allow designers to break complex
systems into smaller specialized modules.

15
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.310
These chiplets can be
manufactured separately

16
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.860
and assembled into
a high-performance package.

17
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.940
Package sizes can go
beyond the reticle limit.

18
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.050
Moreover, package size and wiring
density are projected to grow rapidly,

19
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.320
providing headroom for growth
and investment protection.

20
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.280
This modular approach offers
significant advantages,

21
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.150
lower manufacturing costs, improved
yields, and the flexibility

22
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.560
to reuse as well as mix and match
chiplets for different applications.

23
00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.280
However, there are also
challenges to consider.

24
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.650
Chiplet-based systems can incur
higher package costs and higher

25
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.540
testing costs compared
to traditional monolithic designs.

26
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.900
Additionally,
the interoperability challenge,

27
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.440
especially when integrating
chiplets from different vendors.

28
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.740
How do chiplets connect?

29
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.440
Packaging plays a critical role.

30
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.040
Different methods like 2D, 2.5D,

31
00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:54.380
and 3D stacking enable efficient chiplet
integration depending on the needs.

32
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.290
Leading companies like Intel,
AMD, and NVIDIA have already

33
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.000
adopted chiplet-based architectures
with applications expanding into AI,

34
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.100
cloud computing, and consumer electronics.

35
00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.890
Industry analysts agree
the market for chiplet ecosystems

36
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.280
is growing at a rapid rate with widespread
adoption across enterprise and compute,

37
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.880
communications, industrial, consumer
electronics, and automotive industries.

38
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.090
In this series of courses,
we'll explore the technology

39
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.860
and challenges to be solved
in the areas of chiplet architectures,

40
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.840
packaging technologies,
die-to-die interfaces,

41
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:39.200
cost structures, and the growing
open chiplet economy.

42
00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.980
Are you ready to dive in?

43
00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.450
Let's explore the world of chiplets

44
00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.460
and unlock the future
of semiconductor innovation.

45
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:53.200
[gentle music]

